# Status and money

## Table status columns

Use `type: 'status'` with `meta.variantMap` — never custom `render` with `<StatusBadge>`.

Helper: `statusColumn(key, header, variantMap)` from `@/components/data/columns`.

```tsx
// shared.tsx
const CLIENT_STATUS_MAP = { Active: 'success', Prospect: 'info', … } as const;

export const clientColumns: CrudColumn<ClientRecord>[] = [
  {
    key: 'status',
    header: 'Status',
    sortable: true,
    type: 'status',
    meta: { variantMap: CLIENT_STATUS_MAP },
  },
];
```

Reuse the same map in detail page `subtitle` and DetailView field values.

## StatusBadge elsewhere

```tsx
<StatusBadge status={row.status} variantMap={CLIENT_STATUS_MAP} />
```

Import from `@/components/feedback/StatusBadge`. Never inline `<Badge variant={…}>` for record status.

## Currency display

Use `<MoneyText>` from `@oktavius/base-ui` — never local `formatMoney()` helpers.

```tsx
// ✅ detail fields, StatCard values, table currency columns
<MoneyText value={client.annualRevenue} currency="EUR" />

// ✅ CrudTable — use column type
{ key: 'total', type: 'currency', align: 'right', meta: { currencySymbol: '€' } }
```

```tsx
// ❌ don't copy per module
function formatMoney(v: string) {
  return `€ ${Number(v).toLocaleString('de-AT', …)}`;
}
```

Defaults: EUR / `de-AT` locale. Use `compact` for large dashboard KPIs.
